WEBVTT

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.690
Dining is war.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.650
Humans versus food: it's eat or be eaten!

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.660
But enough of that!

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.870
En garde!

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.670
Not a single noodle will escape me!

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:28.170
Come! To war!

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.930
<i>July.</i>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.480
<i>The blazing sun.</i>

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.110
<i>The shining blue waves.</i>

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.610
<i>The beautiful clear skies...</i>

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.280
<i>...is what I'm currently painting.</i>

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.500
<i>We have exams coming up.</i>

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.370
<i>So we're indoors for summer lessons.</i>

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.090
Hey, Misaki, what are you guys painting?

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.880
You're <i>both</i> doing watermelons?

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.630
Have some imagination!

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.260
At least paint a beach with people splitting them or something—

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.800
If we accidentally do the sea...

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.140
It'll just remind us of how terrible our lot in life is now!

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.390
R-Really?

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.900
How about you, Machiko?

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.900
Mine's a watermelon too.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.950
How's that supposed to be watermelon?

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:03.410
Pickled watermelon rinds are incredibly tasty.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.160
I-If you say so.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.830
We only get one summer vacation!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.040
We shouldn't be wasting it like this!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.130
But we have exams coming up.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:20.260
If we don't work hard this summer, we may not be able to enjoy ourselves next summer.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.800
Plus, think of it this way: our allowances will last for longer than last year's.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.760
Huh? Why?

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.480
We're indoors all day, so we don't need sunscreen.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.600
I don't even use that stuff to begin with!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.980
So how does that do me any good?!

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:39.740
But Morino, you've been able to stay over at Machiko's since summer classes started.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.900
I guess.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.450
So what's the problem?
Aren't you having fun?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:49.250
We haven't had time for a barbecue or shaved ice party because of all this homework, though!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.500
We haven't even been to the Star Festival fair,

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.000
so we haven't made any summer memories at all!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.210
Then why not come over to my place tomorrow?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.260
So, we visit you?

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.430
Yeah.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.510
I think we can put together something summer-ish.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.520
Something summer-ish?!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.780
You're expecting way, <i>way</i> too much.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.450
I can't wait to go visit Shiina.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.080
Me too.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.250
What are you writing, Kirin?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.800
I thought I'd write down some summer-ish things.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.350
I don't think museums and zoos have much to do with the season.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.680
Yeah, but I added in the places I wanted to go during summer vacation.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.850
Here are the things everyone can agree mean summer.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.350
The fireworks, and the pool, and the bug bites.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.860
Do bug bites really count as a thing?

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:04.950
Shiina said "something summer-ish", so I wonder how many we'll be able to get through.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.490
All of them if we're lucky?

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.540
I don't think mountain climbing or trips to the sea are in the cards.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.200
I dunno, she seemed pretty confident.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.790
Plus, she's loaded, right?

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:20.550
I've taken classes with her since eighth grade, but there's still a lot I don't know about her.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.090
I'm sure the scenery will be gorgeous, though.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.840
Oh, that's right!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.800
Kirin?

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.680
Ta-dah!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.890
I'll bring my swimsuit, just in case!

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.020
Really? We're just going to her house.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.230
But she's rich, right?
So she has to have a pool.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.530
She might have a Doberman too.
We need to make sure we don't get bitten.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.030
Just who do you think Shiina is?

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.080
This is...

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.330
Shiina's place?

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.460
Hello, this is Machiko Ryo.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.210
I have an appointment with Shiina, uh, I mean, with your daughter—

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.380
It's me. Come in.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.970
Okay!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.470
This place is huge.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.470
It's hard to believe just one family lives here.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.270
Ooh, there's a garden!

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.440
Though I guess that's pretty normal.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.030
Hi. Are you Shiina's mom?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.030
Are you sure?

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.160
Thanks a lot!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.790
Ryo! Shiina's mom...

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:42.210
I'm sorry! I'm Morino Kirin!

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:49.930
Welcome.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.840
Thanks for having us over.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.470
This is an amazing old mansion.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.100
My family's been here since my great-great-grandfather.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:02.360
Kirin! Where'd you get that tomato?

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:05.320
You can't just take whatever you see.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.400
Well excuse me!

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.450
Shiina's mom was in that garden,
and she gave it to me!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.030
But no one's there.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.120
What?

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.870
No, Mom's gardening.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.500
What is that garden, anyway?

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.250
It's Mom's hobby.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.960
She used to sell what she grew, but...

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.250
Oh, by the way,

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:28.590
Morino, be careful in there.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.970
There are traps.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:34.430
Traps? In ?

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:38.100
That should count as a zoo!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.560
I'm not sure that's the whole zoo experience.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.560
Close enough.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.360
Oh hey, Shiina, do you have a pool?

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.360
Well, no,

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.570
but we do have a pond.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:50.950
Eek! It has a face!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:54.410
Ghost koi apparently used to be a thing.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.910
We've had him for a while,
and he's gotten pretty big.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.580
So? Want to swim?

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.080
I... think I'll pass.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.080
Oh, that's the aquarium visit too.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:10.340
Actually, I think that's closer to the ghost stories...

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.890
The deck is super huge too!

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.680
I'm going to go get some tea.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.230
Mom said she wanted to meet you, too, so wait here.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.270
Okay.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.860
This is amazing.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.490
Even the carvings of the window panels are so delicate...

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.280
I've never seen hanging scrolls like these!

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.910
There's your art museum, then.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:44.710
Silly Ryou. No matter how impressive it is, a house isn't a museum.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.710
<i>What was that awkward laugh for?</i>

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.500
Where is Shiina's mom, anyway?

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.460
I still need to thank her for that tomato.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.220
What's she like, anyway?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.220
She's just like Shiina. In looks, and especially in personality.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:06.480
So, quiet and serious, and a bit cool and mysterious?

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.610
Sorry to keep you waiting. This is my mother.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:17.620
Why, hello there! Pleased to meet you!

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.160
Wow, she's cute!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.870
Huh, who was that before, then?

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.620
Shiina, you have such wonderful friends!

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.340
Thanks for always being there for her.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.210
I'm Machiko.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:34.760
Shiina has also been a good friend to me.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.930
I'm Morino Kirin.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.430
A pleasure to meet you as well!

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.180
What's she doing?

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.270
Kirin acts extremely proper around grownups.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.690
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.940
What a polite young lady!

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.280
Anyway, you finally made it over,
so I want you to go ahead and relax.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.200
Oh, that's right! Snacks!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.660
Here you go!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.120
Shortcake and cheesecake,

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.330
Sachertorte and kuzumochi.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.580
I've got summer presents for you too!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:13.960
Hot spring buns from the neighbors, maple leaf buns, and wine buns!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.220
It's not even lunchtime yet, Mom.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.510
Well, isn't that too bad. I guess you'll just have to take them home with you?

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:20.850
Well...

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.510
Thank you so much!

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.640
See, Ryo?

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.480
There's all the sweets I can eat!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.850
Kirin...

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.900
Hm? What's in that notebook?

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.780
Summer-ish things?

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.190
How about having flowing somen in the courtyard?

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.650
Flowing somen?!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.410
I've only ever seen that on TV.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.080
Can you do it here?

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:48.000
Yep. It takes a lot of work to set up, but it'll be really memorable!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.960
Why don't you go pick a bamboo stalk?

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.590
Pick a bamboo stalk?

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.800
I'm not sure we're in Tokyo anymore.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.010
All right, we can mark off going to the forest!

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.180
Wait, I never wrote that down.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.060
You two should also pick one.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:11.150
Look for one that's thick,
but also nice and straight.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.060
Okay.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.570
Thick and straight,
thick and straight...

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.860
Kirin?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:25.080
Oh, I was just wondering who I saw in the garden.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.160
You mean the person who gave you the tomato?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:27.950
Yeah.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:31.830
She looked just like Shiina,
except she was wearing a kimono.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.840
A kimono? Not many people wear those anymore.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.260
Look, a grave.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:46.430
It's unusual to find graves on mansion grounds.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.850
You'd really need a lot of land.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.020
Hold on, could she have been...

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.770
A ghost?

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:58.900
Well, I guess you did have "ghost stories" written down.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:01.740
Seriously. She vanished into thin air.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.910
She looked just like Shiina, but she was wearing a kimono like they did in the old days...

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.740
Is she one of Shiina's ancestors?!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.980
How about this one?

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.070
Shiina!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.740
Wait for me, Kirin!

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.280
What's going on?

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:49.660
We found a real ghost!

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.420
It followed us here!

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.170
Oh, that's Tsuyuko.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.050
She's one of our helpers.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.670
Pleased to meet you.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.170
<i>Th-They look so much alike!</i>

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.300
Mom was really busy with work when I was little,

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:10.180
so she's always been there for me.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.560
Oh, that makes sense.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.140
Silly Kirin.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.940
Hey, you believed it too!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:20.070
I think this is the one we want,
Tsuyuko. Can you cut it?

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.690
Understood.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.250
That looks fun!

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.620
Would you like to try?

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.540
For real?

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.510
It's so hard!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.730
It's so heavy!

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.780
It's so hot...

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.000
You two need to take it easier.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.420
Here, have some water.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.340
They're so cute and energetic!

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.430
You two almost gave yourselves heat stroke.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.760
You should rest there for a while.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.550
Okay!

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.720
Sorry.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:38.020
Tsuyuko, would you mind helping me set up—

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.520
Hold it right there!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.690
Look at how red your hands are!

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:43.820
It's noth—

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.530
Tsuyuko! Fetch the ointment!

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.280
Here.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.570
Now let me see your hands.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:50.820
You've got splinters too!

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:51.740
Like I said—

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.830
Tsuyuko, fetch the tweezers!

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.740
Here.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.950
Where did she pull that out of?

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:00.210
Good skin is vital for girls!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:00.920
But...

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.080
No "buts" from you, young lady!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.550
Even Shiina's overwhelmed.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:06.090
Moms are tough.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.300
Anyway.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.260
Ryo?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.970
I'm going to go start on the somen.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.520
You still need to rest.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.810
I'll be inside, so I should be fine.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.650
Even I can help boil somen!

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.980
Then I'll take care of things out here.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.730
Tsuyuko, could you lend them a hand in the kitchen?

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:28.490
As you wish.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.740
Somen cooks in the blink of an eye,

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.700
so first, we'll make the dipping sauce.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.460
Let's start with a conventional base of kelp and tuna.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.000
It smells great!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:46.000
I like to add egg yolk to my sauce!

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.170
That sounds wonderful.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:52.590
We'll also be adding Shiina's homegrown tomatoes to create a sauce with a light, Mediterranean feel.

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.260
Of course, we can't forget tradition,
so we'll also be making sesame sauce.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.680
Gently grind the sesame...

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.440
Done.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:04.810
Wow, it's ground to a perfect paste!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.400
The texture is so delicate!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.190
It's amazing!

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:10.070
Tsuyuko, you're a hyper helper!

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.150
It's nothing.

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.280
You really are!

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.070
You're beautiful too! I hope I can be like you when I grow up.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.620
Did we make her mad?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:20.250
So that's why she ground the sesame so fast.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.410
Sounds like my dad—

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.460
Is there anything else?

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.460
Oh, right, the garnish...

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.710
Of course, I'll chop some leek.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:31.590
She's fast!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.880
She really is a hyper helper!

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:36.140
Wow, look how many she's chopped.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.100
These are still connected...

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:45.350
Forgive me. Your praise made me want to show off.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.110
Okay, here they come!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.620
Ready!

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:02.790
I'm ready anytime!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.790
What are you doing, Machiko?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.790
Kirin told me we were supposed to eat like this.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:12.210
Oh, is she giving you weird ideas again?

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.300
Not a single noodle will escape me!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:21.430
Wow, she's really hyped up. This should be fun.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:25.440
I'm sorry, I'm not really familiar with the etiquette of eating flowing somen.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:29.190
It's hard to get much in large groups,

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:32.820
but there's only three of us today so it should be fine.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.570
Okay.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.080
The flow of the water is so beautiful and elegant...

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:47.580
That's right. It's really something to be enjoyed in a more relaxed manner.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.840
The sound of flowing water is wonderful too.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.720
Calming sounds for the ears,
and refreshing sights for the eyes...

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.840
Huh?

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.890
The most important part, the noodles, aren't here yet.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.270
I wonder why?

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:08.480
<i>I forgot about the impenetrable wall known as Kirin.</i>

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:12.940
<i>Not a single noodle will escape me!</i>

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.410
Yay, I got some!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:38.930
The thick, rich egg and the slippery dipped noodles are just incredible!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.560
It's cooling me off so well!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.640
The bite of the leek is so refreshing too!

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:57.190
<i>Compared to the hot, muggy weather, it's like a breeze of fresh air.</i>

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:02.660
<i>Phew. My daughter isn't the only one who eats like that.</i>

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.580
Mixing up the sauces is nice too.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.920
The sesame sauce is so thick and rich.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.920
That's the last of the noodles.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.090
Say what?

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:16.420
I was just getting started!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.880
Shall we boil some more?

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.010
I'll take care of it.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:20.840
Don't worry about it.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.550
No fair, noodles! I wanted more!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.520
Thanks for coming over today.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:31.440
We should be thanking you,
for being such a wonderful host.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.810
I'm sorry we dropped by on such short notice.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:39.440
Honestly, it was my idea for her to invite you over.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.450
Huh?

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.030
Shiina's seriously shy.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.700
She has a hard time staying on the same page with others.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.710
I've been worried that she doesn't have many friends.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:56.710
But lately she's been talking a lot more about her life.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.470
When I asked her about it, she couldn't stop talking about you two.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:05.470
Ryo, Kirin, I hope you two stay friends with her.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.560
Of course!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.060
No problem!

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.060
What did I miss?

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.310
Welcome back!

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.320
I-I'm not sure I trust those smiles.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:26.910
It's beautiful.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.000
We're a bit late, but still,
no better time than the present.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.660
Star Festival time!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.330
It's gotten dark, so why don't we set off some fireworks?

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.880
We have watermelons too!

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.920
I brought the lanterns.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.680
Hurray!

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.680
I see.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:51.180
This is definitely summer-ish.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.900
Fireworks, the Star Festival, watermelons...

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.270
This is feels like a fair...

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:04.200
Wow, that's all of them!

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.080
Aw, it fell off again.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.080
What am I supposed to do with these?

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.580
You have to hold them real steady.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:23.130
Shiina's family gets along so well.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.760
Yeah.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.050
Summer's great, isn't it?

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.260
Yeah! Summer's the best!

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.270
I'll heat up the bath when we get back.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.150
Great idea.

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:40.650
Hey, let's pick up a nice, soothing bath bomb on the way home.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.530
It's nice not having to see you off.

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.080
Hm? What's wrong?

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:51.540
Oh, nothing.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.290
<i>Summer vacation isn't over yet.</i>

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.040
<i>Even if we don't get to go very far,</i>

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:07.050
<i>I know this will be a very special summer for me.</i>

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:45.570
Next time, we'll get to try a lot of tasty things.

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:50.360
If I had to mention one in particular,
it would be this cool, sweet ice cream—

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:51.950
Wrong.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:52.990
Tsuyuko?!

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:56.370
Ice cream is at least 15 percent milk solids.

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.700
Ice milk is between 10 and 15 percent.

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:03.710
And what you're describing now,
which also uses vegetable oils, is—

00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:06.380
Next time on Gourmet Girl Graffiti!

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.800
Hot and Springy!
